Privacy Policy - Quick Socials
Last Updated: April 11, 2026

The Quick Socials extension is designed with a strict focus on user privacy. All operations are performed locally on your machine.

DATA COLLECTION The Quick Socials does not collect, store, or transmit any personal data, browsing history, or identifying information to any external servers.

USE OF PERMISSIONS The extension requests the "tabs" permission for the sole purpose of identifying if a tab you are trying to open is already active. This information is processed entirely in memory and is never recorded or shared.

THIRD-PARTY SHARING We do not collect any data, and therefore have no data to share with third parties. We do not use any analytics or tracking scripts.

LOCAL COMMUNICATION The extension communicates exclusively with the locally running Quick Actions Stream Deck application via a WebSocket bridge (localhost). No data ever leaves your local network.

CONTACT & UPDATES We may update this policy occasionally. Any changes will be reflected by the "Last Updated" date at the top of this page.

